{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524998-vampire-city-situations","id":1524998,"title":"Vampire - City Situations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-03T16:47:18-07:00","id":1524998,"title":"Vampire - City Situations","content":"A fairly popular idea I\u2019ve seen repeated on these forums over the years is the idea that one of the central purposes of the \u2018[City] by Night\u2019-line of books should have been designed with the intent of communicating to the storytellers of vampire a variety of systems and circumstances which they could use to run their own chronicles. It\u2019s also a fairly common opinion that the majority of the city-setting books failed to do this.<br /> <br /> What I propose is a combination thought experiment and inspiration building exercise. Let\u2019s imagine that the notion described above is one of the guiding principles we have in laying out the plan for an imaginary line of city setting books. I encourage people to share any ideas they have for concepts of what a city archetype might look like and bonus points if you have any particular examples in mind for it. <br /> <br /> For example\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Chicago</b><br /> Chicago is largely considered to be the best done of the By Night series and so I think it\u2019s a good place to start with. Chicago by Night in general is praised as a great crash course for new storytellers and players alike about how VtM can be done in practice. The only short coming of that I\u2019d say is that other styles of play never got fledged out as well in later entries imo but that\u2019s not a fault of Chicago itself. Anyway! Chicago\u2019s core structure is that of a Camarilla City with a strong Anarch Presence. In particular it describes a city with a Powerful Primogen Council and Weak Prince*. Furthermore Chicago provides us with some solid mundane hunters (of both the FBI &amp; religious variety), although these are individual-vigilante hunters and not the organized groups some may prefer. Chicago is the birthplace of the \u2018sleeping methuselahs running secret games\u2019 trope which became so endemic to Vampire writing, which, while not a bad idea in and of itself and in Chicago I think it\u2019s done fairly well offers a compelling vehicle for Jyhad-level plots, I do feel that it was overdone as time went on. We needed more ways of showing how the Jyhad effects life in a city then just giving every city one or two sleeping methuselah (or antediluvian as the case may be). Plus Chicago is early enough in the lifecycle of WoD that the more odd things like having a random Succubus running around is still possible and I think that the WoD is better for it.<br /> <br /> <b>Washington, DC</b><br /> I\u2019ve got a soft spot for this book because it was my first city book and I grew up near DC, but it has its issues. It\u2019s strongest element though might be that it provides a clear reversal of the Chicago Situation: DC had a Strong Prince and Primogen so weak they sometimes feel like an afterthought. It shows how such a powerful prince might handle things differently than a prince in Lodin\u2019s situation and that\u2019s useful. Of course the Secret Lasombra and Secret Sabbat things kind of muddy the water but Marcus Vitel still gets a pass for doing it first imo (if we can give Helena &amp; Menele a pass than Sejanus gets one too). I think it also handles the lupine connection fairly well and I like the Black Magic night club even though we don\u2019t really get that much about it. One of this book\u2019s biggest failings imo is not doing more to integrate DC as a vampire setting. It\u2019s the capital of the US and the book was written in the afterglow of the Cold War when the US was the undeniable global hegemonic superpower and could proudly declare history to be over; more could have been done to integrate themes such as these into the game alongside how vampires maintain their influence and masquerade with such proximity to the levers of government. It also would be a good place for some page count to be given to how the Camarilla and the Technocratic Union interact imo but unfortunately all we get is assurances that NWO snipers will take down any vampires who try to blood bond the Speaker of the House. That\u2019s fine I guess but I wish we had more, y\u2019know?<br /> <br /> Those are some of my own examples. I might add some more later. Hopefully people can share some of their own ideas for city structures or scenarios that it would have been worthwhile to see her a book!<br /> <br /> *\u2019Weak\u2019 here should be real as comparatively weak. Lodin is the archetypal prince in VtM for a reason, he\u2019s quite solid. He\u2019s just comparatively weak in Chicago\u2019s politics because of the overwhelming power of the Primogen when acting collectively. Lodin\u2019s struggles to try to undermine or alter that relationship makes great potential story fodder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}